      "title": "source/testplan/testplan-introduction.xml",
      "pageStart": null,
      "pageEnd": null,
      "target": "../sections/s001-source-testplan-testplan-introduction-xml.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "```xml\n<div xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\" xsi:schemaLocation=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml ../../schema/fhir-xhtml.xsd\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">\n\n<div>\n<a name=\"bnc\"></a>\n<h2>Scope and Usage</h2>\n<p>\nThe TestPlan is a canonical resource that defines how an system or specifications (which can be represented by FHIR artifacts or by narrative) are to be tested. It contains the business- and planning-language aspects of test planning, around the TestScript, which handles part of the test execution.\n</p>\n<p>A TestPlan describes the purpose, the dependencies, sco",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The FHIR R5 build-source introduction to TestPlan. Scope and Usage: TestPlan is a canonical resource defining how a system or specification is to be tested, covering the business and planning side around TestScript, which handles part of execution. It describes purpose, dependencies, scope, test environment, framework and output, and holds test cases with entry criteria (preconditions), exit criteria and test data or instructions for obtaining it, supporting traditional and agile (TDD, BDD) testing. Test plans can depend on or extend others for reuse, e.g. a national specification requiring conformance to IHE profiles, WHO datasets, ISO IDMP and OpenHIE. Boundaries: TestPlan says what to test and is maintained from a business perspective, TestScript says how to test; a TestPlan can be tied to any canonical resource, including a whole ImplementationGuide or some of its artifacts.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-31"
      }
    },
