      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The FHIR 5.0.0 StructureDefinition for TestPlan (draft, maturity 0, FHIR Infrastructure, a specialisation of CanonicalResource described as 'a plan for executing testing on an artifact or specifications'). Besides the canonical metadata elements (url, identifier, version, versionAlgorithm, name, title, a required status, experimental, date, publisher, contact, description, useContext, jurisdiction, purpose, copyright, copyrightLabel) it defines category, scope (what is tested), testTools, dependency (description and predecessor), exitCriteria, and testCase with sequence, scope, dependency, testRun (narrative, or a script with language such as gherkin or testscript and source), testData (a required type such as 'synthea', content and source) and assertion (type, object, result). It also carries the cnl-0 and cnl-1 warning constraints on name and url.",
